            "mimeType": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
            "text": "{\"data\":{\"event0\":{\"event_id\":\"93e23aab-9d4a-4c04-9454-63a22980eb58\",\"description\":\"An experimental film that does not revise history but temporarily suspends it. A true work of art.\\n\\nTickets include popcorn. Drinks will be available from the bar all evening. \\n\\nJoin us when the doors open so you have time to meet fellow film lovers, catch up, and share your guesses about what the mystery film might be!\\n\\nDoors open: 6:30pm \\nFilm start: 8pm\\n\\n18+ only event \\n\\nNote: We’ll be taking photos and videos during the event for online use. If you’d prefer not to appear in any of them, just let us know.\\n\\nAll tickets are non-refundable. You’ll have the ability to resell your ticket on the platform if the event sells out.\"},\"event1\":{\"event_id\":\"4d11dc26-e304-4e4f-bf2c-4f499e9c6fbe\",\"description\":\"Cinebug’s first horror screening: Alien by Ridley Scott! See it on 16mm film, projected old-school style in an intimate setting. A night to remember!\\n\\n15 seats only – so act fast!\\n\\nYour ticket includes drinks and snacks.\\n\\nCiné Real, E5 0NS\\n\\nEvent start: 7:00 PM\\nScreening start: 7:30 PM\\n\\nNote: Doors will be locked at 7:30 PM and there is no reception inside. If you’re running late, please message us in advance, and we’ll do our best to accommodate.\\n\\nTickets are not refundable. You'll have the ability to resell your ticket on the platform once the event sells out.\"},\"event2\":{\"event_id\":\"a2efc9f4-e0e9-4e75-a7ae-5f12ab115cf9\",\"description\":\"Our first private screening of 2026 will be a mystery one! \\n\\nAn ordinary boy and an extraordinary bond create a quietly powerful British classic by one of the nation’s most acclaimed directors.\\n\\nTickets are £5 and include popcorn. The Little Yellow Door food & drinks menu will be available to order all evening.\\n\\nDoors open: 7pm Film start: 8pm\\n\\n18+ only event \\n\\nNote: We’ll be taking photos and videos during the event for online use. If you’d prefer not to appear in any of them, just let us know.\\n\\nAll tickets are non-refundable. You’ll have the ability to resell your ticket on the platform if the event sells out.\"},\"event3\":{\"event_id\":\"3d9abd05-b26e-490a-ac4d-def6d86c1986\",\"description\":\"One of my favourite cinema experience in 2025 was seeing Hamnet at the London film festival. The power of human connection and storytelling was at its purest. \\n\\nIt’s finally time to experience it together on release day Friday 9th January 20:35 at BFI Southbank.\\n\\nMake sure to BOOK YOUR TICKET DIRECTLY ON THE BFI’s WEBSITE (we’re sitting in K23) and then book your free ticket on here to let us know you’re coming and to get updates. \\n\\nhttps://whatson.bfi.org.uk/Online/mapSelect.asp\\n\\nWe’ll meet from 7pm in the BFI café/bar to catch up before the screening. \\n\\nSee you there !\"},\"event4\":{\"event_id\":\"56b9bc7b-d78f-432a-805c-f2e90f9b5879\",\"description\":\"Join us at All is Joy in Soho for a special screening of Singin' in the Rain and our end of year social! \\n\\nThanks to Cinema For All, tickets are £3 only and include a hot drink by Ada café !\\n\\nArrive from 6:30 pm to mingle at the bar, then settle in for a cozy, classic cinema experience (film starts at 7:30pm). \\n\\nAfter the credits roll, we’ll head back to the bar to toast the holiday season, celebrate the highlights of 2025 releases and talk about the films we look forward to in 2026.  \\n\\nDon’t miss this perfect mix of movies, new friends, and festive cheer! It’s the ultimate way to wrap up the year! \\n\\nNote: We’ll be taking photos and videos during the event for online use. If you’d prefer not to appear in any of them, just let us know\\n\\nAll tickets are non-refundable.\"},\"event5\":{\"event_id\":\"b564ec24-eb44-41b2-8135-d2f9c1380be5\",\"description\":\"Cinebug is very excited to announce that we’re teaming up with Florence Rose for a special, intimate screening of The Holdovers on December 18th at one of our favourite places, Blown Away Studios.\\n Come early to enjoy festive drinks, snacks, and to get to know each other. Then cozy up and watch this new classic with us. See you soon! ✨\\n\\nEvent Details :\\nDoors open 6:30pm Film starts 8:00pm\\nEnd of event approx 10pm\\n\\nNote: We’ll be taking photos and videos during the event for online use. If you’d prefer not to appear in any of them, just let us know\\n\\nAll tickets are non-refundable. You’ll have the ability to re sell your ticket on the platform if the event sell outs.\"},\"event6\":{\"event_id\":\"1ba19bcb-90d2-4dd4-9622-02f6b6bbf09c\",\"description\":\"FRAME BY FRAME × TURNING PAGES\\n\\n\\nRead. Watch. Discuss.\\n\\nBook club meets cinema club for a special first-time collaboration! Join us for an hour of reading before our screening of the cult classic; The Perks of Being a Wallflower.\\n\\nWe recommend you bring a book that’s been adapted for the screen (to go with the theme), but if you’re in a flow with a certain book, that’s totally fine. We’ll then settle in for the film - before the night rolls on with drinks, conversation, and DJs.\\n\\nA Thursday night made for book lovers and cinefiles alike\"},\"event7\":{\"event_id\":\"4c9a2cbb-32c8-445b-bf15-57c219d95a11\",\"description\":\"Ho ho Ho-ldovers! We’re ending the year back at ALL IS JOY for a spectacular night of cinefile Christmas fun. Want a pub quiz film can actually win? This one’s for the Letterboxed lovers and pop culture pros \\n\\nCome alone or come as a team - either way, it’s gonna be a good one\\n\\n📅 When: Friday 5th December\\n📍 Where: All Is Joy\\n🕕 Doors: 6:15pm\\n🎟️ Tickets: £5\"},\"event8\":{\"event_id\":\"c2dc69c9-d649-4413-acdb-e0e413b54f54\",\"description\":\"We’re teaming up with A24 for our members to attend the UK premiere of ETERNITY. \\n\\nWith Filmmaker David Freyne and actors Miles Teller, Elizabeth Olsen, John Early and Da’vine Joy Randolph!\"},\"event9\":{\"event_id\":\"d078bfa3-7382-4ac7-a9ef-96c31c8b937d\",\"description\":\"In partnership with new gallery GALLERIA OBJECTS we’re hosting an afternoon where art, coffee and cinema come together in a celebration of all things culture! We’re screening the acclaimed Cannes winning and BAFTA nominated PORTRAIT OF A LADY ON FIRE. So grab your friends or come for the perfect solo date\\n\\nDOORS: 4:00PM \\nSCREENING: 4:30PM\"},\"event10\":{\"event_id\":\"487e93b0-53ef-49b6-9e59-736edea3c62a\",\"description\":\"FRIDAY 22ND OF AUGUST \\nSCREENING: HOW TO HAVE SEX (FEATURE) \\nUs Man Dere - REBIRTH (SHORT) \\nQ&A with ENVA LEWIS \\n\\n📍all is joy soho \\n🚪6:45pm\\n🎬7:30pm\"},\"event11\":{\"event_id\":\"7d8ee2c8-c038-45bd-bda8-aa7cbf67743c\",\"description\":\"⚠️ IMPORTANT ⚠️ Please only RSVP if you’re planning to actually attend the screening! Cinema tickets are not included with this RSVP. Please book it via the Picturehouse website as per the description.\\n\\nJoin us for a screening of Wuthering Heights at Picturehouse Ritzy!\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nSaturday, 14 February from 12:45. The movie starts at 13:20, but no stress if you’re running late, with trailers first, you’ll be fine arriving up to 20 minutes after!\\n\\n📍 WHERE\\nBrixton Oval, Coldharbour Ln, London SW2 1JG\\n\\n🎟️ HOW TO JOIN\\n1) RSVP to this event to join the group chat (make sure you’ve downloaded the CLIQ app). We’ll use it to coordinate where to meet and share the ticket link for the correct showing.\\n2) Book your seat. We're in K12!\\n3) Send a quick message in the chat to confirm you’re attending with your seat number.\\n\\n📝 SYNOPSIS\\nWuthering Heights follows the obsessive, all-consuming love between Catherine Earnshaw (Margot Robbie) and Heathcliff (Jacob Elordi), whose bond is torn apart by class, pride, and betrayal in 18th-century England.\\n\\n💬 WHAT TO EXPECT\\nOur cinema hangouts are super casual, think of them as a way to watch a film with great company! We’ll meet before the screening to chat, head in together, and share a few thoughts afterward. \\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n⋆ Connect with fellow cinephile women in a friendly, no-pressure environment.\\n⋆ No need to be an expert, just bring your thoughts, feelings, and love for film.\\n⋆ Discover (or re-discover) cinema together.\\n⋆ Find your third space: a comfy in-between for connection, creativity, and community.\\n\\n📌 QUICK INFO\\n⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t be shy, our community is warm and welcoming!\\n⋆ This event is open to the women+ community.\\n⋆ Any Qs? Drop me a message, always happy to help!\"},\"event12\":{\"event_id\":\"0869a49a-67a2-453f-a497-da52ad8dad04\",\"description\":\"Join us for this month’s Pick of the Month: our cosy, conversational meetup (book club-style) where we come together to unpack Hamnet (dir. Chloé Zhao)!\\n\\nWe’ll meet in the sofa area of the BFI Bar (Upstairs), the perfect setting for an easygoing chat about the film’s themes, emotions, and whatever else comes up.\\n\\n★ First hour: You’ll join a small group with a tailored set of discussion prompts.\\n★ Second hour: We’ll mingle, swap groups, and explore a new set of questions.\\n\\n⚠︎ Please watch the film beforehand, we’ll be jumping straight into discussion ⚠︎\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nSaturday, 21st of January from 14:00 to 16:30 (ish)\\n\\n📍 WHERE\\nBFI Bar (Upstairs by the Mediatheque), Belvedere Rd, London SE1 8XT\\n\\n📝 SYNOPSIS\\nWilliam Shakespeare (Paul Mescal) and his wife, Agnes (Jessie Buckley), celebrate the birth of their son, Hamnet. However, when tragedy strikes and Hamnet dies at a young age, it inspires Shakespeare to write his timeless masterpiece \\\"Hamlet.\\\"\\n\\n💬 WHAT TO EXPECT\\nOur monthly film discussions take place on the second Saturday of each month (this month delayed by a week). We vote on the film, watch it separately, then come together to discuss it book-club style, with guided prompts, a live recommendations board and plenty of chances to mingle.\\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n⋆ Connect with fellow cinephile women in a friendly, no-pressure environment.\\n ⋆ No need to be an expert, just bring your thoughts, feelings, and love for film.\\n ⋆ Discover (or re-discover) movies together.\\n ⋆ Find your third space: a comfy in-between for connection, creativity, and community.\\n\\n┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈\\n\\nFAQ’s\\n ⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t be shy, our community is warm and welcoming!\\n ⋆ This event is open to the women+ community.\\n ⋆ All ticket sales go towards supporting the running of The Film Club.\\n ⋆ Any Qs? Drop me a message, always happy to help!\"},\"event13\":{\"event_id\":\"af7dfc2b-1a54-4d87-b087-225ec0b94f5e\",\"description\":\"⚠️ IMPORTANT ⚠️ Please only RSVP if you’re planning to actually attend the screening! Cinema tickets are not included with this RSVP. Please book it via the Regent Street Cinema website as per the description.\\n\\nJoin us for a screening of The Social Network at Regent Street Cinema!\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nSunday, 22 February from 12:30. The movie starts at 13:00, but no stress if you’re running late, with trailers first, you’ll be fine arriving up to 20 minutes after!\\n\\n📍 WHERE\\n307 Regent St., London W1B 2HW\\n\\n🎟️ HOW TO JOIN\\n1) RSVP to this event to join the group chat (make sure you’ve downloaded the CLIQ app). We’ll use it to coordinate where to meet and share the ticket link for the correct showing.\\n2) Book your seat. We're in F6!\\n3) Send a quick message in the chat to confirm you’re attending with your seat number.\\n\\n📝 SYNOPSIS\\nMark Zuckerberg (Jesse Eisenberg) creates a social networking site, Facebook, with his friend Eduardo's (Andrew Garfield) help. Though it turns out to be a successful venture, he severs ties with several people along the way.\\n\\n💬 WHAT TO EXPECT\\nOur cinema hangouts are super casual, think of them as a way to watch a film with great company! We’ll meet before the screening to chat, head in together, and share a few thoughts afterward. Just to set expectations, this is a casual group hangout rather than a private or hosted screening. We don’t make reservations or organise activities before or after the film. \\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n⋆ Connect with fellow cinephile women in a friendly, no-pressure environment.\\n⋆ No need to be an expert, just bring your thoughts, feelings, and love for film.\\n⋆ Discover (or re-discover) cinema together.\\n⋆ Find your third space: a comfy in-between for connection, creativity, and community.\\n\\n📌 QUICK INFO\\n⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t be shy, our community is warm and welcoming!\\n⋆ This event is open to the women+ community.\\n⋆ Any Qs? Drop me a message, always happy to help!\"},\"event14\":{\"event_id\":\"345c2a8b-9331-4434-a6cf-85de04b70cce\",\"description\":\"⚠️ Limited spots! ⚠️ Only sign up if you’re sure you can make it.\\n\\nJoin us for a relaxed, cosy night in with fellow cinephiles as we watch the BAFTAs together! Hosted by Maggie, a Film Club member, this is the perfect way to celebrate the films and performances everyone’s talking about, while enjoying snacks, drinks, and good company.\\n\\n✨ Expect…\\n⋆ Live streaming of the BAFTAs in a chill, comfy setting\\n⋆ Snack & drink potluck, bring something to share!! 🍿🥤\\n⋆ Casual, friendly hangout vibe with chatting, laughs, and film talk\\n⋆ Low-key social atmosphere perfect for mingling and celebrating cinema\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nSunday, 22 February | 18:30-21:30 (BAFTA ceremony runs approximately 19:00-21:00)\\n\\n📍 WHERE\\nScape Hammersmith, 181 Talgarth Road, London W6 8BJ\\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n⋆ Celebrate film, performances, and the BAFTAs with fellow cinephiles\\n⋆ Share snacks, sip drinks, and enjoy a relaxed, fun night\\n⋆ Connect with the Film Club community in a casual, no-pressure setting\\n\\n📌 QUICK INFO\\n⋆ This is a potluck event, bring a snack or drink to share!\\n⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t worry if you’re coming alone\\n⋆ Open to the women+ cinephile community\\n⋆ Any Qs? DM us anytime!\"},\"event15\":{\"event_id\":\"fbec1e4c-7abc-405d-844c-bbf907c00019\",\"description\":\"Join us for a cosy Oscar Predictions night as we guess the winners of the 2026 Academy Awards. We’ll fill out prediction cards together, and the sharpest forecaster on awards night will take home a prize ✨\\n\\nWe’ll meet in the sofa area of the BFI Café/Bar, the perfect setting to chat through the nominees, make our predictions, who we wish would win, and unpack the year’s biggest snubs.\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nSaturday, 7th of February from 14:00 to 16:30 (ish)\\n\\n📍 WHERE\\nBFI Café/Bar (Upstairs by the Mediatheque), Belvedere Rd, London SE1 8XT\\n\\n💬 WHAT TO EXPECT\\nA cosy, low-pressure space to talk all things Oscars. You’ll take part in small-group chats about who will win, who should win, and who was snubbed, with plenty of time to mingle, meet new people, and keep the conversation going. We’ll swap groups in between so you get even more chances to connect! \\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n⋆ Connect with fellow cinephile women in a friendly, no-pressure environment.\\n⋆ No need to be an expert, just bring your thoughts, feelings, and love for film.\\n⋆ Discover (or re-discover) movies together.\\n⋆ Find your third space: a comfy in-between for connection, creativity, and community.\\n\\n┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈\\n\\nFAQ’s\\n ⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t be shy, our community is warm and welcoming!\\n ⋆ This event is open to the women+ community.\\n ⋆ All ticket sales go towards supporting the running of The Film Club.\\n ⋆ Any Qs? Drop me a message, always happy to help!\"},\"event16\":{\"event_id\":\"043a4044-4f6e-4876-9352-2edfa83cfd51\",\"description\":\"⚠️ IMPORTANT ⚠️ Event tickets are not included with this RSVP! Please book it via the BFI website as per the description.\\n\\nJoin us for a full day at the Women With a Movie Camera Summit at BFI Southbank! This annual event celebrates and explores the work of women filmmakers, featuring inspiring talks, panels, and discussions with creatives across the industry. Check out the full schedule on the BFI website.\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nSaturday, 24th December from 11:00. If you’re joining a bit later, just use the chat to find the group.\\n\\n📍 WHERE\\nBFI Southbank, Belvedere Rd, London SE1 8XT\\n\\n🎟️ HOW TO JOIN\\n1) Buy your ticket to the Summit via the BFI website. \\n2) RSVP to this event to join the group chat (make sure you’ve downloaded the CLIQ app).\\n3) Let us know in the chat that you’re coming, ticket in hand and ready to go!\\n4) We’ll use the chat to coordinate where and when to meet on the day, and to help everyone find each other throughout the day.\\n\\n💬 WHAT TO EXPECT\\nWe’ll get together and then dive into the sessions that interest us most. We might break into smaller groups depending on which talks we want to attend. Later, we’ll regroup over coffee to share thoughts, chat about highlights, or just hang out and soak up the day together. A relaxed, friendly way to explore the summit and spend a day with fellow film lovers!\\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n⋆ Connect with fellow cinephile women in a friendly, no-pressure environment.\\n⋆ No need to be an expert, just bring your thoughts, feelings, and love for film.\\n⋆ Discover (or re-discover) cinema together.\\n⋆ Find your third space: a comfy in-between for connection, creativity, and community.\\n\\n📌 QUICK INFO\\n⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t be shy, our community is warm and welcoming!\\n⋆ This event is open to the women+ community.\\n⋆ Any Qs? Drop us a message, we're always happy to help!\"},\"event17\":{\"event_id\":\"3e06f77f-3008-4dee-be89-3bbcf2728cbe\",\"description\":\"⚠️ IMPORTANT ⚠️ Please only RSVP if you’re planning to actually attend the screening! Cinema tickets are not included with this RSVP. Please book it via the BFI website as per the description.\\n\\nJoin us for a screening of Breathless at BFI Southbank!\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nFriday, 23 January from 18:10. The movie starts at 18:30, but no stress if you’re running late, with trailers first, you’ll be fine arriving up to 20 minutes after!\\n\\n📍 WHERE\\n BFI Southbank, Belvedere Road, South Bank, London SE1 8XT\\n\\n🎟️ HOW TO JOIN\\n1) RSVP to this event to join the group chat (make sure you’ve downloaded the CLIQ app). We’ll use it to coordinate where to meet and share the ticket link for the correct showing.\\n2) Book your seat. We're in L22!\\n3) Send a quick message in the chat to confirm you’re attending with your seat number.\\n\\n📝 SYNOPSIS\\nPetty thug Michel (Jean-Paul Belmondo) considers himself a suave bad guy in the manner of Humphrey Bogart, but panics and impulsively kills a policeman while driving a stolen car. On the lam, he turns to his aspiring journalist girlfriend, Patricia (Jean Seberg), hiding out in her Paris apartment while he tries to pull together enough money to get the pair to Italy. But when Patricia learns that her boyfriend is being investigated for murder, she begins to question her loyalties.\\n\\n💬 WHAT TO EXPECT\\nOur cinema hangouts are super casual, think of them as a way to watch a film with great company! We’ll meet before the screening to chat, head in together, and share a few thoughts afterward. \\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n⋆ Connect with fellow cinephile women in a friendly, no-pressure environment.\\n⋆ No need to be an expert, just bring your thoughts, feelings, and love for film.\\n⋆ Discover (or re-discover) cinema together.\\n⋆ Find your third space: a comfy in-between for connection, creativity, and community.\\n\\n📌 QUICK INFO\\n⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t be shy, our community is warm and welcoming!\\n⋆ This event is open to the women+ community.\\n⋆ Any Qs? Drop me a message, always happy to help!\"},\"event18\":{\"event_id\":\"250a97b2-5c39-4798-a4ab-4e5a89ca5f30\",\"description\":\"🎉 The Film Club turns 2! 🎉\\n\\nWe’re celebrating in style with a surprise film screening, fun mingling games, and of course, plenty of cake! Join us for an unforgettable evening hosted inside a Shoreditch art gallery, where you can connect with fellow cinephiles, enjoy a female-directed gem, and toast to two amazing years of The Film Club.\\n\\n✨ Expect...\\n⋆ A private screening of a female-directed surprise film (very TFC coded, if I must say...)\\n⋆ Popcorn to enjoy during the screening. \\n⋆ Cupcakes and special Birthday themed touches throughout the night 🍿\\n⋆ A complimentary celebratory cocktail to cheers (optional, if you drink) to 2 years of The Film Club! \\n⋆ Post-screening social with mingling games to spark conversation and connection\\n⋆ Great film chat, new pals, and a warm, artful atmosphere\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nSunday, 18th January | 16:30 to 20:00 (ish) | Film starts at 17:00\\n\\n📍WHERE\\nGalleria Objects, 92 Brick Ln, London E1 6RL\\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n⋆ Connect with fellow cinephile women in a friendly, no-pressure environment.\\n⋆ No need to be an expert, just bring your thoughts, feelings, and love for film.\\n⋆ Discover (or re-discover) cinema together.\\n⋆ Find your third space: a comfy in-between for connection, creativity, and community!\\n\\n📌 QUICK INFO\\n⋆ Seating is on standard chairs as this is a community space, please bring additional layers if you’d like to be extra comfy.\\n⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t be shy, our community is warm and welcoming!\\n⋆ This event is open to the women+ community.\\n⋆ All ticket sales go towards supporting the running of The Film Club.\\n⋆ Any Qs? Drop me a message, always happy to help!\"},\"event19\":{\"event_id\":\"08828a21-39ac-41d2-ba4a-8547a6e4d1c6\",\"description\":\"Join us for this month’s Pick of the Month: our cosy, conversational meetup (book club-style) where we come together to unpack Marty Supreme (dir. Josh Safdie)!\\n\\nWe’ll meet in the sofa area of the BFI Café/Bar, the perfect setting for an easygoing chat about the film’s themes, emotions, and whatever else comes up.\\n\\n★ First hour: You’ll join a small group with a tailored set of discussion prompts.\\n★ Second hour: We’ll mingle, swap groups, and explore a new set of questions.\\n\\n⚠︎ Please watch the film beforehand, we’ll be jumping straight into discussion ⚠︎\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nSaturday, 10th of January from 14:00 to 16:30 (ish)\\n\\n📍 WHERE\\nBFI Café/Bar (Upstairs by the Mediatheque), Belvedere Rd, London SE1 8XT\\n\\n📝 SYNOPSIS\\nMarty Supreme (2025) follows Marty Mauser (Timothée Chalamet), a brash, ambitious New Yorker in the 1950s determined to make table tennis famous, and himself even more so. Loosely inspired by real ping-pong player Marty Reisman, the film charts Marty’s rise from obscurity to international competition, blending sports drama, comedy, and a character study of ego, ambition, and the cost of chasing greatness.\\n\\n💬 WHAT TO EXPECT\\nOur monthly film discussions take place on the second Saturday of each month. We vote on the film, watch it separately, then come together to discuss it book-club style, with guided prompts, a live recommendations board and plenty of chances to mingle.\\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n⋆ Connect with fellow cinephile women in a friendly, no-pressure environment.\\n ⋆ No need to be an expert, just bring your thoughts, feelings, and love for film.\\n ⋆ Discover (or re-discover) movies together.\\n ⋆ Find your third space: a comfy in-between for connection, creativity, and community.\\n\\n┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈┈\\n\\nFAQ’s\\n ⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t be shy, our community is warm and welcoming!\\n ⋆ This event is open to the women+ community.\\n ⋆ All ticket sales go towards supporting the running of The Film Club.\\n ⋆ Any Qs? Drop me a message, always happy to help!\"},\"event20\":{\"event_id\":\"3e333271-06bb-4ef4-9434-d8b8ad36ec54\",\"description\":\"Join us for a one-of-a-kind screening of Little Women (2019), Greta Gerwig’s tender, spirited adaptation of sisterhood, ambition, art, and the intertwined lives of the March women, hosted inside a Shoreditch art gallery!\\n\\nAfter the film, join us for a post-screening social where we’ll chat about creativity, girlhood, the film’s layered storytelling, and the timeless comfort of returning to the March sisters again and again.\\n\\n✨ Expect...\\n⋆ Private screening of Little Women at an art gallery\\n⋆ Post-screening social with gentle icebreakers to spark conversation and connection\\n⋆ Complimentary popcorn, desserts and special themed elements throughout the night 🍿📚\\n⋆ Great film chat, new pals, and a warm, artful atmosphere\\n\\n📅 WHEN\\nSunday, 14th December | 17:30 to 21:00 (ish) | Film starts at 18:00\\n\\n📍WHERE\\nGalleria Objects, 92 Brick Ln, London E1 6RL\\n\\n📝 SYNOPSIS\\nIn the years after the Civil War, Jo March reflects on her life with her three sisters, Meg, Amy and Beth, each determined to carve out her own path. As they navigate love, loss, art, and independence, their stories intertwine in a richly emotional portrait of womanhood.\\n\\n💬 WHAT TO EXPECT\\nOur Cinema Club series brings you to hand-picked London cinemas for intimate screenings (sometimes private, sometimes specially curated) always followed by a social designed to spark conversation and connection.\\n\\n🎟️ WHY JOIN?\\n ⋆ Connect with fellow cinephile women in a friendly, no-pressure environment.\\n ⋆ No need to be an expert, just bring your thoughts, feelings, and love for film.\\n ⋆ Discover (or re-discover) movies together.\\n ⋆ Find your third space: a comfy in-between for connection, creativity, and community.\\n\\n📌 QUICK INFO\\n ⋆ Most attendees come solo, so don’t be shy, our community is warm and welcoming!\\n ⋆ This event is open to the women+ community.\\n ⋆ All ticket sales go towards supporting the running of The Film Club.\\n ⋆ Any Qs? Drop me a message, always happy to help!\"},\"event21\":{\"event_id\":\"4ab07b96-d857-40d5-9819-b04b698b895e\",\"description\":\"🎀 Galentine’s Movie Afternoon 🎀\\n\\nCome celebrate Galentine’s Weekend with the girls at a cosy movie afternoon 💌\\n\\nWe’re watching the ultimate rom-com classic When Harry Met Sally at Prince Charles Theatre 🍿✨\\n\\nA fun, relaxed way to meet new girls, hang out, and enjoy a throwback movie together - perfect if you’re coming solo or with friends.\\n\\n📍 Prince Charles Theatre\\n🗓 Sunday 15th February\\n⏰ Meet at 2:20 PM\\n🎬 Movie starts at 2:45 PM\\n\\nFollow us @girlswhowalkldn on Instagram\"},\"event22\":{\"event_id\":\"800224a9-d6a2-4606-9e2d-534f0d8f1347\",\"description\":\"🚴‍♀️ GWW x Psycle RIDE – London Bridge 🎶\\n\\nJoin us at the brand new Psycle studio in London Bridge for their signature RIDE class.\\n\\nRIDE is Psycle’s signature cardio experience on a bike — low impact, high intensity, and synced to the rhythm of the music. Designed to strengthen body and mind, this class builds endurance, floods you with feel-good energy, and leaves you feeling lighter.\\n\\nWe’ll be joining one of Psycle’s main classes together, so expect amazing music, big studio energy, and a serious sweat 💦\\n\\n🗓 Saturday\\n⏰ 10:00 AM class\\n\\n💸 £20 per person \\n\\n⸻\\n\\nWhat to bring\\n\\nWear something comfortable to sweat in and bring a water bottle. Cleated shoes are provided.\\n\\n⸻\\n\\nStudio Check-In\\n\\nPlease arrive at least 15 minutes before class to check in and get set up.\\nAny spaces not checked in 4 minutes before the class start time will be released.\\nNo late entry once the class has started.\\n\\n⸻\\n\\nCome solo or with friends — everyone is welcome 💛\\n\\nFollow us for more events 👉 @girlswhowalkldn\"},\"event23\":{\"event_id\":\"7aebba94-d13f-4d47-9838-b6ab8b21403c\",\"description\":\"GWW x Ketobee Walk 🍃\\n\\nJoin us for a relaxed Girls Who Walk x Ketobee morning, focused on movement, connection, and feel-good energy ☀️\\n\\nWe’ll meet at Ketobee to kick things off before heading out on our walk together.\\n\\n✨ Ketobee drinks available to purchase (matcha, smoothies & more)\\n✨ Complimentary samples of Ketobee’s keto cookie to try\\n\\nCome solo or with friends, everyone is welcome.\\n\\n📍 Ketobee, 372 King’s Road, SW3 5UZ\\n⏰ Meet at 11:00 AM\\n🚶‍♀️ Walk to Battersea Park\\n\\nFollow us on Instagram @girlswhowalkldn\"},\"event24\":{\"event_id\":\"de725d91-40d3-406b-b15c-18583a24533f\",\"description\":\"💙 Girls Who Walk x Walk for Understanding \\n\\nEating Disorders Awareness Week Fundraiser\\n\\nWe will be joining ‘Walk for Understanding’ in Hyde Park to support Eating Disorders Awareness Week alongside other communities and groups across London.\\n\\nThis is a mixed-gender charity walk bringing people together to raise awareness, show compassion, and support those affected by eating disorders.\\n\\n🗓 28th February 2026\\n⏰ 10:00 AM\\n📍 Meet at Speakers’ Corner (Marble Arch)\\n🚶‍♀️ 5km walk through Hyde Park\\n\\nEveryone is welcome to join us for this important cause.\\n\\nFollow us for more community events 👉 @girlswhowalkldn\"},\"event25\":{\"event_id\":\"8efb507c-6538-47ca-826f-65654006b5ab\",\"description\":\"🎨 GWW x The Art Social – Ceramic Painting Night ☕✨\\n\\nJoin us for a cosy, creative evening at Green House Coffee with The Art Social.\\nThis relaxed ceramic painting session is perfect for switching off, getting creative, and meeting lovely new girls in a warm café setting.\\n\\nNo experience needed — all abilities welcome. Just come ready to paint, chat, and unwind.\\n\\n🗓 12th March\\n⏰ 7:00 PM – 8:45 PM (arrive 10 mins early)\\n📍 Green House Coffee\\n🎟 £16 per person (excl food/drinks to be purchased on the day)\\n👯‍♀️ 16 spaces\\n\\nFollow us 👉 @girlswhowalkldn\"},\"event26\":{\"event_id\":\"2d211228-3ed3-4f65-ab5b-445e84de8ba7\",\"description\":\"Breakfast Club at Timmy Green ☕️\\n\\nJoin us for our monthly Breakfast Club at Timmy Green ☕🥐\\n\\nA relaxed morning to meet new girls, enjoy good food, and connect.\\n\\n📍 Timmy Green\\n🗓 Saturday 7th February, meet at 11:30 AM\\n\\nEveryone welcome 🤗 Follow us @girlswhowalkldn on Instagram\"},\"event27\":{\"event_id\":\"96b7fa7b-15a9-41e3-89a7-79561feae60a\",\"description\":\"🚶‍♀️ Battersea Park Walk\\n\\n🗓 Saturday 31stJanuary, meet at 11:00 AM\\n📍 Pear Tree Cafe\\n\\nJoin us for a relaxed Saturday morning stroll through one of London’s most beautiful parks. Perfect for a slow start to the day, good chats, and soaking up some greenery in the city.\\n\\n✨ Everyone welcome – follow us on Instagram @girlswhowalkldn ✨\"},\"event28\":{\"event_id\":\"e7de41a0-0fb6-46fe-a231-72d76fb8d8c7\",\"description\":\"🌿 Mindful Yin Yoga & Wellbeing Session 🌿\\n\\n📅 24th January\\n⏰ From 3:00 PM onwards (please arrive by 2:50 PM at the latest)\\n🧘‍♀️ Duration: 90 minutes\\n\\nStart your 2026 right with a calming and beginner friendly session of yoga with Sadhana Wellbeing Studio ✨\\n\\n• Yin Yoga class\\n• Q&A and chat session with some tea\\n\\nTerms & Conditions: \\n\\n• Mats are included.\\n• Arrive at least 10 minutes before class.\\n• Bring water (refill stations available or water can be purchased at reception).\\n• Wear suitable sports clothing (leggings or shorts).\\n• Your full name, email address, and phone number will be shared to register you on the Momence app for class access. By purchasing a ticket, you agree to us creating an account on your behalf.\\n\\nFollow us on Instagram @girlswhowalkldn 🫶\"},\"event29\":{\"event_id\":\"a256f67f-e726-41b7-b5c3-9a9dee546802\",\"description\":\"Girly Dinner & Drinks 🍷✨\\n\\n📍 Tuesday 20th January, 8:00 PM\\n📍 Tiny Wine, Fitzrovia\\n\\nJoin us for a relaxed evening of dinner, drinks, and good company 💞\\n\\nWe’ll be heading to Tiny Wine, a newly opened wine bar in Fitzrovia, for cozy vibes, great wine, and girly chats 🍷\\n\\nWith limited spaces available, this is the perfect midweek plan to unwind and enjoy a cute night out ✨\\n\\n🎟 £14 per ticket\\n💷 £10 off your individual bill on the day\\n💺 Limited spaces available\\n\\nCome solo or with a friend — everyone’s welcome 🤍\\n\\nFollow us on Instagram @girlswhowalkldn 🫶\"},\"event30\":{\"event_id\":\"347d55ec-05ff-4d92-95b5-089628da5a6a\",\"description\":\"Walk, Pastry & Coffee ☕🥐🚶‍♀️\\n\\n📍 Saturday 10th January, 11:00 AM\\n📍 Meet at Mama & Sons Café, Kentish Town\\n\\nJoin us for a relaxed walk and coffee morning 💞\\n\\nWe’ll meet at Mama & Sons, a Kentish Town bakery serving up delicious Filipino-inspired comfort food, before heading on a short stroll to Primrose Hill for some fresh air and good vibes 🌿\\n\\nMama & Sons are also launching their new range of juices and shakes, so come ready to try something new 🧃\\n\\n🥐 Free pastries & coffee\\n🚶‍♀️ Easy-paced walk\\n☕ Fun chats & community\\n\\nCome solo or with a friend – everyone’s invited 🤍\\n\\nFollow us on Instagram @girlswhowalkldn 🫶\"}}}\n",
